@startuml
title Stable Hydration State and Transient Operations
skinparam shadowing false

state "CLOUD_ONLY\nDB namespace exists\nno complete physical content" as Cloud
state "HYDRATING\ntransient operation" as Hydrating
state "HYDRATED\nDB namespace exists\nvalid physical content exists" as Hydrated
state "DEHYDRATING\ntransient operation" as Dehydrating
state "LOCAL CHANGE\nphysical content must be preserved" as Dirty

[*] --> Cloud : remote item recorded\non-demand, no local requirement
Cloud --> Hydrating : content demand / always_local
Hydrating --> Hydrated : validated content materialised\nthen stable DB state committed
Hydrating --> Cloud : failure / cancellation\nno valid final backing file

Hydrated --> Dirty : user/local modification
Dirty --> Hydrated : existing sync completes\nremote/local state reconciled

Hydrated --> Dehydrating : explicit/policy request\nonly after safety checks
Dehydrating --> Cloud : physical removal safe\nthen stable DB state committed
Dehydrating --> Hydrated : abort/failure\npreserve content

note right of Dirty
Dirty is not a candidate for
automatic dehydration.
end note
@enduml
